#
# Conformance case: derivation/indirect-contributor
#
# AC: a cross-slice derivation rule's head appears in the native materialization.
#
# input.nq models a provenance generation chain as DATA: an entity gmeow:wasGeneratedBy
# an activity that gmeow:wasAssociatedWith an agent. The rule composes the two hops.
#
# The rule under test — a monotone positive-Horn logic:Rule mirroring the production
# logic:ruleIndirectContributor (gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ∘ gmeow:wasAssociatedWith ⇒
# gmeow:indirectContributor). Every head variable is a frontier variable bound positively
# in the body, so it lowers to an evaluable rule and the chase DERIVES its head:
# materialized.nq is a strict superset of input.nq carrying the derived
# gmeow:indirectContributor edge — proof the derivation materializes (logic:ExactPreservation),
# not SoundUnderApproximation residue.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/derivation/indirect-contributor/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# gmeow:wasGeneratedBy(entity, activity) ∧ gmeow:wasAssociatedWith(activity, agent)
#   ⇒ gmeow:indirectContributor(entity, agent)
ex:ruleIndirectContributor
    a logic:Rule ;
    logic:provenance ex:ruleIndirectContributor ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?entity" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:indirectContributor ;
        rdf:object    "?agent"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?entity" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ;
        rdf:object    "?activity"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?activity" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:wasAssociatedWith ;
        rdf:object    "?agent"
    ] .
